description: Build page layout convention (BuildShell)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Build pages

- URL shape: `/{category}/{build}` (e.g. `/birthday/slider`). Never put a build at a bare category root.
- Category pages live at `/{category}` (e.g. `/birthday`) — a simple directory: small logo, category nav, builds listed as shortcuts. Do not redirect category roots into a build.
- Categories are listed in `src/lib/builds.ts` (`categories`) in sidebar order. Empty categories are allowed for scaffolding.
- Site root `/` redirects to the default category (`/birthday` for now).
- Build **title** is the short build name only (e.g. `slider`), not `birthday slider`. Category lives in the path.
- Use `BuildShell` (`src/components/build-shell.tsx`) for every experiment/build route. Pass `backHref` to the category page.
- Title + description at the **top** (centered).
- Interactive build content is vertically + horizontally centered in the **remaining space below the header** — never absolutely centered over the full viewport (that overlays the title).
- Top-left back pill → category page. No logo on build pages.
- Metadata titles use hyphen separator: `%s - buildwithduy`.
- Creator filming mode: same build URL with `?creator=true`. No title/description. Small form (name + when were you born). Birth year field opens a modal with the build in **year-only** mode. Wire pages through `BuildExperience`.

# Registry + sitemap

- Register every public build in `src/lib/builds.ts` (directories + sitemap). After each new build: create `src/app/{path}/page.tsx`, add the `builds` entry, confirm category + build URLs appear in `/sitemap.xml`.

# Build shortcut thumbnails

- Every build gets a demo thumbnail in `src/components/{name}-demo.tsx`, wired through `BuildShortcut`.
- Thumbnails must animate **inside the card on hover**, driven by the parent Link’s `group` / `group-hover:` classes (same pattern as slider thumb slide and angry-cake flight).
- Idle state shows a quiet preview; hover plays a short motion that hints at the interaction. Prefer CSS transitions or keyframes — no autoplay loops while idle.
- Birthday (and any date-showing) thumbnails always use **today’s date** via `formatToday` / `getTodayParts` from `src/lib/today.ts` — never a hardcoded or random date. Use `suppressHydrationWarning` on the date text.
- When adding a new build: ship the hover thumbnail animation with the build, not as a follow-up.
